  "verbalization": "Arillanin A appears to interact with Neuropilin-2 through a series of molecular pathways, with the target relationship established through multiple indirect links. The first pathway connects Arillanin A to Solute carrier family 12 member 5, which is then targeted by Harman-3-Carboxylic Acid and ultimately by Neuropilin-2. The second pathway links Arillanin A to Solute carrier family 12 member 5, which is targeted by 2-Hydroxyemodin 1-Methyl Ether, which in turn targets Neuropilin-2. The third pathway connects Arillanin A to UDP-glucuronosyltransferase 2A1, which is targeted by a compound that targets Neuropilin-2. These pathways suggest that Arillanin A may influence Neuropilin-2 through different molecular mechanisms, possibly involving the regulation of transporters or enzymatic activities. The integration of these evidence strands highlights a potential role for Arillanin A in modulating Neuropilin-2 function, though the exact mechanism remains to be elucidated.",
